00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.910
So first, API services--

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.720
here, you can see a super
high-level overview that

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.750
shows where the platform sits.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:39.150
And the Apigee Edge runtime sits
in between your API consumers

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.920
and your back-end systems.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:45.930
And this facade pattern allows
you to extract or abstract

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.270
a lot of the cross-cutting
concerns that you would

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:51.570
typically be building into
your back-end services--

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:55.930
things like security,
throttling, managing SLAs

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.609
with particular clients.

00:03:58.609 --> 00:04:00.150
All of these types
of things that you

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.880
have to do for all of
your API consumers,

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.800
you move those
into the platform.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.770
And then that frees up
your service developers

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:11.370
to focus on building
services that are related

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.475
to their domain expertise.

00:04:13.475 --> 00:04:15.600
And they don't have to
worry about implementing all

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.808
those cross-cutting concerns.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.660
