trial situation--

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:28.100
then I'll move on
somewhere else.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.450
So having that world-class
developer experience

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:33.070
is really important.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.890
Additionally, in the
developer services,

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:41.950
we host things inside your
portal, like a forum, blogs.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:43.250
We can host SDKs--

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.670
all of the typical
things that API consumers

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:49.657
expect to help them leverage
your APIs and be successful.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.980
And then finally,
analytics services--

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:57.260
so you've built out your APIs.

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.420
They're being
consumed, hopefully

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:02.790
by a lot of developers,
both internal and external.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:05.810
So how do you measure the
success of your program?

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:10.580
How do you know which APIs
are experiencing greater

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.500
than expected latency?

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.605
Are there high error
rates for particular APIs?

00:06:15.605 --> 00:06:18.500
Is that a problem with
your API, your API

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:23.880
documentation, your back end, or
is it an issue with the client?

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.420
So with Apigee
Analytics, we provide

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:30.470
you insights all the way
from the client consuming app

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.100
to your back-end service.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.940
So you can see everything
